docs {
  # Admin - Get Report Details
  
  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/admin/reports/:id`
  **Auth:** Required (Admin Access Token)
  
  ## Description
  Retrieves comprehensive report details by ID including populated reporter, reported user, and reviewing admin profile information.
  
  ## Request
  
  ### Headers
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`) |
  
  ## Response
  **`200 OK`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "reporter_user_id": 1,
      "reporter_user": {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "Ali Rezaei",
        "email": "ali@example.com"
      },
      "reported_user_id": 2,
      "reported_user": {
        "id": 2,
        "name": "Spammer",
        "email": "spam@example.com"
      },
      "reason": "HARASSMENT",
      "description": "User is sending offensive messages repeatedly.",
      "status": "PENDING",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-02T19:00:00Z"
    }
  }
  ```
  ## Errors

  * `400 Bad Request` — Invalid report ID format
  * `401 Unauthorized` — Missing or invalid token
  * `403 Forbidden` — Insufficient permissions (requires ADMIN role)
  * `404 Not Found` — Report not found
}
